      children: [(0,jsx_runtime.jsx)(_components.strong, {
        children: "Osho Darshan:"
      }), " The priest and the general — the two poles of the ancient world — are both his. Osho says the divine is not a specialist: it is present as the wisdom of the counselor and the courage of the commander. The ocean among lakes teaches the last lesson of this shloka: every lake is a small ocean; every quality is a small infinity. The devotee must learn to see the ocean in the lake, the infinite in the finite — that seeing is the whole of spiritual maturity."]
